# ============== Secrets — NEVER commit these ==============
# Anything env-shaped, not just the two names that were listed. A migration
# backup called .env.repo-before-migration matched neither `.env` nor
# `.env.*.local`, so it was a tracked path holding four live credentials —
# caught by check_no_secrets before it reached a commit, which is luck rather
# than design. The old repository was deleted over exactly this kind of leak.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
# (.env.example IS tracked — it's the template, no real values)
!.env.example

# ============== Runtime / generated data ==============
# Live trade history, balances, open positions, audit logs.
# Everything in data/ is per-machine state; keep template only.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# Logs
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep
*.log

# Backups
*.bak

# ============== Python ==============
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Virtualenv
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# pytest / coverage / linters
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ============== macOS / Windows / IDE ==============
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# ============== Optional: keep config templates in repo ==============
config/watchlist.json.bak
# config/watchlist.json is NOT tracked. src/watchlist_updater.py rewrites it
# every week from the momentum ranking, so a tracked copy is a per-machine
# runtime product that shows up as a diff on any machine the refresh has run
# on — the file's own header already says hand edits get overwritten.
#
# It IS required at startup: main.load_watchlist() reads it with a bare
# read_text() and dies on a missing file (staging hit exactly that), and
# packaging/mmt-backend.spec bundles config/*.json as the templates seeded
# into the app home. So a fresh clone must generate one — run the universe
# refresh — before the bot or a packaged build will come up.
config/watchlist.json

# ============== Databases — private, never a source file ==============
# Everything the bot writes already lives under data/, which is ignored above.
# These are the second line: a trader.db copied to the repo root to inspect it
# is still live trade history, and build.sh's secret scan already refuses to
# ship a bundle containing one. SQLite keeps -wal/-shm sidecars beside the file
# and they hold committed rows, so they go wherever the database goes.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# ============== Signing material ==============
# *.pem and *.key are at the top with the secrets. These are the rest of what a
# signing identity is: the app is ad-hoc signed today, but a Developer ID
# certificate exported for notarisation is a .p12 with a private key inside.
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest

# ============== Release images ==============
# macos/.gitignore already covers dist/. This catches an image built or copied
# anywhere else — 122 MB each, and they belong on a GitHub release, not in git.
*.dmg

# ============== Swift / Xcode local state ==============
# Absent while the build goes through `swift build`, but both appear the first
# time macos/Package.swift is opened in Xcode.
.swiftpm/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate

# ============== macOS strays / merge leftovers ==============
# ._* are AppleDouble resource forks, written whenever the repo touches a
# non-APFS volume — a USB stick, some network shares. Icon? is the custom
# folder icon Finder writes. *.orig and *.rej are what a failed merge or a
# rejected patch hunk leaves behind.
._*
Icon?
*.orig
*.rej

# ============== Compiled / temp ==============
*.tmp
*.temp

# Parameter change journal — per-install runtime record, like logs/. The
# parameters themselves (config/parameters.json) ARE tracked: seeing what a
# value changed to, and when, is the point of keeping them in one file.
config/parameters_history.jsonl
